\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces WA-FGNG{} separates four operations. Depth samples are transformed with a supplied camera pose, retained in a bounded world-voxel memory, replayed without repeated-view multiplicity, and represented by a foveated graph. The memory budget $K$, replay budget $S$, and graph budget $B$ are distinct. Geometry in this architecture diagram is schematic; experimental renderings use recorded benchmark outputs.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{2}{\method {} separates four operations. Depth samples are transformed with a supplied camera pose, retained in a bounded world-voxel memory, replayed without repeated-view multiplicity, and represented by a foveated graph. The memory budget $K$, replay budget $S$, and graph budget $B$ are distinct. Geometry in this architecture diagram is schematic; experimental renderings use recorded benchmark outputs}{figure.1}{}}
